All in [/live/Live.js](/framework/files/?path=live/Live.js), 150 lines, four classes.

**Live** extends #Page. The page itself: owns the log, draws the feed newest first.

**LiveLog** extends JSONL. The delta engine for this page:

```js
content(v){
	const { clear, add, remove, by, ts } = v;
	if (clear) this.items = new Map();
	if (add) this.items.set(add.id, this.stamp({ ...add, by, ts }));
	if (typeof remove === "string") this.items.delete(remove);
}
```

**Tail**. Polls page.jsonl every ~3 s with a byte Range; only new bytes replay. What a socket would replace.

**LiveCard** extends #Page. One row as a small page:

```js
class LiveCard extends Page {
	static live = { today: LiveToday };          // custom renderers, by name
	preview(nav){ return this.preview_card(nav); } // the feed tile
	full(){ /* back link, title, md(this.text) */ }
}
```

A card is a Page. So the registry = Page subclasses picked by `type`.

