Cards open at `/live/<id>/`, full width; code side-scrolls, and `js wrap` opts a block into wrapping.

Every class below lives in one file: [`live/Live.js`](/framework/files/?path=live/Live.js). Each snippet names it at the top.

**Live** is the page (the default export). It extends #Page.

**LiveLog** replays page.jsonl into a Map of cards. Its `content()` is its own replay method, not Page's:

```js
// live/Live.js
class LiveLog extends JSONL {
  content(v){
    const { clear, add, remove } = v;
    if (clear)  this.items = new Map();
    if (add)    this.items.set(add.id, add);
    if (remove) this.items.delete(remove);
  }
}
```

**Tail** polls page.jsonl (the part we're replacing with the socket).

**LiveCard** is one row, a small page:

```js
// live/Live.js
class LiveCard extends Page {
  preview(nav){
    return this.preview_card(nav);
  }
  full(){
    // back link, title, md(this.text)
  }
}
```

Note: on #Page, `content` is NOT a method. It's a getter returning a `PageContent` list (core/Page/PageContent.js). LiveLog's `content()` is a different thing that happens to share the name.

Open question: LiveCard should arguably be its own file, `live/LiveCard.js`.

`live/page.js` is one line, so the page is a singleton:

```js
// live/page.js
import Live from "./Live.js";
export default new Live({
  meta: import.meta,
  title: "Live",
  classes: "hides-nav",
});
```

That one `Live` instance IS the page. Here's the class, trimmed to what it overrides:

```js
// live/Live.js
export default class Live extends Page {
  static Card = LiveCard;  // 3 helpers, named
  static Log  = LiveLog;   // so a subclass
  static Tail = Tail;      // can swap them

  // open the stream ONCE
  start(){
    if (this.stream) return;
    this.stream = new Live.Log({
      url: "./page.jsonl",
    });
    Socket.disabled
      ? new Live.Tail(this.stream, changed)
          .start()          // phone: poll
      : this.stream.live(changed);
                            // desktop: socket
  }

  // newest first; honor `after`
  rows(){ /* ... */ }

  // /live/<id>/ -> a child Page
  route(id){ /* ... */ }

  // draw + redraw on each new line
  mount(box, id){ /* ... */ }

  // one card's full(), or the feed
  paint(id){ /* ... */ }
}
```

The `Socket.disabled` line in `start()` is the socket-vs-poll fork we're widening for your phone.

class-architecture.text:
Three classes, one delta rule, verified from source.

**Item** extends Events. `core/Item/Item.js`. Every value is quarantined in `data`; the instance namespace keeps only id, parent, store, view, Lists, methods.

```js
class Item {
	id; parent; store;
	data = Object.create(null);
	static fields = [];      // accessors over data

	set(k, v){ this.apply(k, v) }   // or set(delta)
	set_one(k, v){
		if (typeof this[k] === "function") return this[k](v);  // method key
		if (this[k]?.set) return this[k].set(v);              // nested delta
		this.put(k, v); this.emit("change"); this.emit("delta");
	}
	get(k){ /* own prop → data[k] → child id in any owned List */ }
	remove(){ this.parent.remove(this.id) }   // removes SELF
	static hydrate(json){ /* any array key → List */ }
}
```

**List** extends Item. `core/List/List.js`. Not the reverse: Page has ~70 methods and add/move/find/remove would collide, so a Page *has* lists.

```js
class List extends Item {
	items = []; owner; name; of;
	get parent(){ return this.owner }
	find(id){ /* shallow, by key */ }
	remove(id){ /* removes a CHILD, not self */ }
	add(x, { after }){ /* announces: emit add + delta */ }
	insert(x){ /* quiet */ }
	move(); order(); replace(); release(); take();
	// no set() override: {"add": …} works via Item.set_one's method rule
}
```

**Page** extends Item. `core/Page/Page.class.js`. id = name. Owns four things.

```js
class Page extends Item {
	pages;     // List of Pages
	children;  // legacy Map view, ~215 callers
	content;   // PageContent extends List, lazy
	store;     // PageLogReader
	static fields = ["title", "icon", "description"];
	// navigation width arrangement surface background type_size
	// land on the page itself, not in data

	set(obj){            // ONE arg, never (k, v)
		this.jsonl_lines.push(obj); this.emit("line");
		this.take_words(obj);
		super.set(obj);
	}
	add(name, child){ /* a child PAGE */ }
	move(url){ /* re-urls the subtree */ }
}
```

So `{"add":…}` sent to a page makes a subpage; a card needs `{"content":{"add":…}}`.

**Delta flow**, one line in, one line out:

```
line → Page.set → Item.apply → set_one per key
     → child.set(nested)  …  → emit "delta"
     → bubbles item → list → owner → Store listener
     → one nested line appended (skipped while replaying)
```

**Subpages**, both built (`Page/doc/subpages.md`):

```js
{"tab":  {"name":"notes"}}          // embedded: a view of this page
{"file": "kid/page.jsonl"}          // referenced: own folder and url
```

Rule since 2026-10-08: a thing *has* a page; it never extends Page.

**Threaded chat** needs no new storage:

```js
class Message extends Item {
	static fields = ["text", "by", "ts"];
	replies;   // a List, hydrated from the array key
}
// one line, routed by set_one all the way down:
{"m3": {"replies": {"add": {"text": "…"}}}}
```

Gaps: deep plain-object merge exists server-side (`Servex/agents/page_tools.js`) but not in browser `set_one`; Page CRUD/move unfinished; `list_experts` is empty so the Page readme's expert line is stale.
